meta {
  name: List guardians
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/guardians?student_id={{studentId}}&primary=true
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.school: eq {{schoolCode}}
  res.body.guardians: isArray
  res.body.count: eq 1
}

docs {
  "Who do we ring about this child, first" - the student_id and primary filters
  together, which is the query an office actually makes. The link created in
  request 09 is what makes the count 1.

  Note which way the filters read: this is the guardians of a student. The
  mirror image, the students of a guardian, is a filter on /students and folder
  08 has it. Neither is a nested route, because a guardian with children in two
  sections belongs to neither section.

  Unfiltered, this returns every guardian the caller may see, which for an
  office account is the whole parent body.
}
